# Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# Only a developer build reads this file - built with `make dev`, or
# `go build -tags dev`. A released binary ignores it entirely: Rook runs shell
# commands against targets with a provider key in the process, so it must not
# take credentials from whatever directory it was pointed at. Check which build
# you have with `rook --version`.
#
# For a release binary, export these in your shell or put them in
# ~/.config/rook/config.yaml instead.

# Provider credentials. Each built-in backend reads its own conventional
# variable, so exporting the one for your backend is all that is needed.
# ZAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: override config fields via ROOK_<PATH> (see configs/rook.example.yaml).
# ROOK_AGENT_MODEL=glm-5.2
# ROOK_DEFAULT_BACKEND=zai
